    Add the TURN 492 acceptance negatives for the rsqrt index and rstd lookup
    
    The hidden verifier now rejects two active segment selectors, no active
    selector, a shifted rounding quotient, a shifted rounding remainder and a
    shifted segment quotient, each re-committed so the only inconsistency is the
    edited field. A table whose encoding differs from the trusted plan is rejected
    by the verifier configuration compare, and the message tampering test also
    covers a changed sample answer and a changed lookup proof value.
    
    The plaintext check scans the fixed-width buffers of the rstd lookup proof,
    outcome and sample messages at eight-byte boundaries for the little-endian
    bytes of every table value followed by sixteen zero bytes; none appears.
    
    partial progress

